sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CLI as Frontend
    participant Reader as Read-only child
    participant Engine as Owned Engine relay
    participant Owner as Lifecycle owner
    CLI->>Reader: Fresh Ready selection + lifetime pipe
    Reader->>Engine: Inspect exact container and generation
    Reader->>Engine: GET logs (tail, since, optional timestamps)
    Engine-->>Reader: HTTP admission
    Reader-->>CLI: Attached (one marker on reattach)
    loop Bounded output and consumer backpressure
        Engine-->>Reader: Multiplexed bytes
        Reader-->>CLI: Payload and timestamp metadata
    end
    Note over Reader,Owner: No mutation lease while following
    Owner->>Engine: Stop or remove owned container
    Engine-->>Reader: EOF or idle after stop
    Reader->>Engine: Verify selected generation
    alt Real EOF and confirmed stopped or absent
        Reader-->>CLI: Exit 0
        alt Restart intent or fresh replacement
            CLI->>CLI: Fresh admission within 30 seconds
            CLI->>Reader: New reader, bounded 1000-line backlog
        else Down or stopped service
            CLI->>CLI: Stopped notice and named end, exit 0
        end
    else Five idle seconds without EOF
        Reader-->>CLI: native_log_stopped_idle, exit 1
    else Changed generation or unexplained EOF
        Reader-->>CLI: Named refusal
    end
    Note over CLI,Reader: Closed stdout exits quietly. Ctrl-C reaps reader.
    Note over CLI,Reader: Frontend loss closes lifetime pipe
